  "text": "The name Finn means white or fair, and it signals wisdom, not skin tone. Heroes of both sexes often bore this name, and it descends from the name carried by the famous Irish hero Fionn mac Cumhaill. The principal Finns were three triplet brothers whose given names were Bres, Nar, and Lothar, and who went by the name Three Finns of Emain Macha. Together they slept with their sister Clothra of Connacht, who bore a son striped in red to show the parts gained from each father. The brothers challenged their own father, the Tara king Eochaid Fedlech, in arms. He defeated them, then died of grief over their loss.",
